1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:15,100
Last is the improper way out: a student who stopped enrolling without an approved leave. Nobody types 'AWOL'; the system flags it from the imported enrollment records.

2
00:00:16,399 --> 00:00:23,600
Graduate School staff signs in.

3
00:00:25,199 --> 00:00:38,500
The AWOL and Residency board flags cases from the source records. The line above counts the cases in each column.

4
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:53,699
Graduate School staff finds Maya Torres's card in AWOL, with the flag's start date and 'Waiting for: Student'. Staff cannot move it; only the student can start a return.

5
00:00:54,799 --> 00:01:17,700
Residence limits apply: for a master's student, five years normal and seven absolute; for a doctorate, seven and nine. Time on leave counts toward residence. Each rule shows its Handbook page.

6
00:01:19,599 --> 00:01:32,399
The card shows the AWOL date, the flag's source, and the last enrolled semester. Graduate School staff has no button yet.

7
00:01:32,599 --> 00:01:40,399
The student, Maya, signs in.

8
00:01:42,099 --> 00:01:52,700
The Return from AWOL page shows the flag, and says registration stays restricted until review.

9
00:02:01,599 --> 00:02:10,600
Maya picks the return semester and last enrolled semester, then writes the intention and reason.

10
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:17,000
Maya checks the summary and sends.

11
00:02:17,199 --> 00:02:28,300
Submitted. The system finds Maya within the maximum residence. The student cannot cancel it, only contact the Graduate School office.

12
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:41,800
Graduate School staff signs in.

13
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:50,500
On the staff board, the card has moved itself to Return review.

14
00:02:50,699 --> 00:02:59,600
The request shows the intention and the residence limits.

15
00:03:08,099 --> 00:03:16,200
Graduate School staff forwards it to the Dean with a note.

16
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:20,200
Forwarded and locked.

17
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:26,900
The Dean signs in to decide.

18
00:03:32,099 --> 00:03:44,800
The Dean finds Maya's card in that column.

19
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:56,200
The Dean drags it to Back in the program; approval restores standing.

20
00:03:56,400 --> 00:04:02,300
The card lands in Back in the program: Maya is active.

21
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:15,700
Graduate School staff signs in.

22
00:04:15,900 --> 00:04:25,800
Staff board: the Academic Coordinator is next owner, since enrollment is a separate step.

23
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:31,600
All four tracker steps are complete.

24
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:42,500
The Registrar list here has one report per approved return. Graduate School staff downloads it and sends it officially.

25
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:54,800
The student, Maya, signs in.

26
00:04:55,000 --> 00:05:05,900
Maya sees the approval. Leave, return and AWOL all ran on the same board, request window and Registrar list.
